# Standalone managed default-profile repository (design only)

No production model root or previous vector schema import. Profile EXACT accepted six fields: profileId cortex-text-small-1536-v1, modelId openai/text-embedding-3-small, dimensions1536, normalization text-nfc-lf-v1, chunking codepoint-1600-overlap-200-v1, indexName by_default_embedding_v1. PROFILE_HASH is canonical six-field hash, not an invented actual revision. Official native embed model unchanged. Numeric vectors finite1536/-0 refused by mutation before storage; vector index dimensions1536.

Schema design example (registered only in future newly reviewed standalone fixture):

```ts
const scope={tenantHash:v.string(),spaceHash:v.string(),ownerHash:v.string()};
fixtureGrants: defineTable({...scope, grantHash:v.string(), epoch:v.number(),
 operatorHash:v.string(), active:v.boolean(), profileHash:v.string()})
 .index("by_grant",["grantHash"]),
fixtureSources: defineTable({...scope, sourceKey:v.string(), sourceHash:v.string(),
 revision:v.number(), epoch:v.number(), profileHash:v.string(), tombstone:v.boolean()})
 .index("by_source",["sourceKey"]),
fixtureChunks: defineTable({...scope, sourceId:v.id("fixtureSources"), chunkKey:v.string(),
 sourceRevision:v.number(), sourceHash:v.string(), profileHash:v.string(), textHash:v.string(),
 tombstone:v.boolean()}).index("by_chunk",["chunkKey"]),
fixtureVectors: defineTable({...scope, sourceId:v.id("fixtureSources"),chunkId:v.id("fixtureChunks"),
 sourceRevision:v.number(),sourceHash:v.string(),profileHash:v.string(), vector:v.array(v.number()),
 receiptHash:v.string(),dispatchIdentity:v.string(),writeKey:v.string(),tombstone:v.boolean()})
 .index("by_write",["writeKey"])
 .index("by_source",["sourceId"])
 .vectorIndex("by_default_embedding_v1",{vectorField:"vector",dimensions:1536,
 filterFields:["tenantHash","spaceHash","ownerHash","profileHash"]}),
fixtureStages: defineTable({accountHash:v.string(),scenarioId:v.string(),dispatchIdentity:v.string(),
 stageHash:v.string(),stageIdentityHash:v.string(),stageIdentityCanonical:v.string(),
 partSequence:v.number(),rawPartDigest:v.string(),privateCanonical:v.string(),trigger:v.string(),sourceEpoch:v.number(),
 grantEpoch:v.number(),createdAt:v.number()}).index("by_dispatch",["dispatchIdentity"])
```

Table validators are necessary Convex primitives, not full semantic validation: every internal repository handler exact-key validates H/ID/Epoch/N from receipt contract, table IDs via corresponding v.id, exact stored profileHash, all scope fields H; createdAt Time. Table writes internal only. Grants/source/chunks provision operator-only internal root action/mutations on verified fixture target, never caller-derived tenant claims. At most1grant/1source/1chunk/E11vector plus at most2stage records per account, no dynamic corpus. fixtureSources owns source revision/hash, chunks own deterministic one-chunk textHash; no canonical request text or vector in public receipt. Source model/chunk profile belongs server constant; deployment/profile epochs bound in account. Sources contain no user data. Unique query via indexes prevents duplicate silently accepted rows; >1 match corrupt/STOP.

```ts
interface RepoFence {binding:BindingV2; tenantHash:H;spaceHash:H;ownerHash:H;
 grantId:Id<"fixtureGrants">;sourceId:Id<"fixtureSources">;chunkId:Id<"fixtureChunks">;
 sourceHash:H;sourceRevision:Epoch;chunkTextHash:H;profileHash:H;dispatchIdentity:H}
writeE11(ctx:MutationCtx, fence:RepoFence, vector:number[], receiptHash:H):
 {kind:"written"|"replay";vectorId:Id<"fixtureVectors">;vectorHash:H}|
 {kind:"denied";reason:"stale"|"scope"|"closed"|"collision"};
readOwned(ctx:QueryCtx,fence:RepoFence,vectorId:Id<"fixtureVectors">):
 {kind:"current";sourceHash:H;sourceRevision:Epoch;vectorHash:H}|
 {kind:"denied";reason:"stale"|"scope"|"closed"};
searchE14(ctx:ActionCtx,fence:RepoFence,queryVector:number[],limit:1):
 Promise<{kind:"current";matches:Match[]}|{kind:"denied";reason:"stale"|"scope"|"closed"}>;
// Full DeleteIntent/result/idempotency API is normative in replay-cleanup.md, not RepoFence.
deleteOwned(ctx:MutationCtx,intent:DeleteIntent):DeleteResult;
```

Match EXACT {sourceKey:H,sourceRevision:Epoch,sourceHash:H,profileHash:H,score:number}; score finite/-0 refused, at most1 match, NO IDs/vector/text/private/tenant/grant in public result. Internal vectorSearch candidate score/id stays private and must validate before hydration. Unscored read receipt never returns vector. The separate ROOT closed-account cleanup/evidence method returns hashes only, with no vector hydration. Public runner result cannot hydrate staging/private tables. Operation fence must match account manifest binding and E11/E14 attempts; write allowed ONLY E11 with first-capture-qualified terminal+money+serving+usage, attachment authority current, exact finite profile vector/hash/native correspondence. E12/E13 have no write path at all. E14 query search permitted ONLY qualified terminal+money+serving+usage/current authority with separately admitted E14 identity, not E11 native-hash reuse. Empty actual proof registry means these methods currently deny closed until qualified facts exist; managed evidence NOT_RUN.

LIVE operation fence checker in inference read/write/search/new-stage mutation/query rereads account, grant, source, chunk by exact IDs; checks operator/grant hash+epoch active, scope equal on all rows, source epoch/revision/hash/profile matches fence/account, !tombstone, chunk sourceId/revision/hash/textHash/profile+scope exact and !tombstone, current window/proof/profile/source flags and !revoked/cancelled/stopped/closed authority. Production source IDs/hashes are never accepted. Current profile epoch may come from account fixed binding and current profile flag; no separate mutable profile alias. Proof actual model can never silently relabel vector profile.

writeKey=H(canonical{account binding, E11 dispatchIdentity, sourceId,sourceRevision,sourceHash,chunkId,chunkTextHash,profileHash}). One transaction checks all fences and unique writeKey; absent -> inserts exactly1vector. Existing exact dispatch/receipt/vectorHash/profile/source tuple -> replay zero writes; differing vector/receipt/current source -> collision zero writes plus explicit STOP-control path. Async native embedding occurs outside mutation; recheck all current records AFTER embedding in write mutation, never rely on before-inference check. A stale/revoked/deleted source yields denied0writes and no vector resurrection.

searchE14: first internal query returns exact fenced snapshot + opaque epoch binding. Action invokes official ctx.vectorSearch("fixtureVectors","by_default_embedding_v1",{vector:queryVector,limit:1,filter:q=>q.and(q.eq("tenantHash",...),q.eq("spaceHash",...),q.eq("ownerHash",...),q.eq("profileHash",PROFILE_HASH))}). Vector index cannot filter source/tombstone; final internal hydrate query therefore rereads account/grant/source/chunk and EVERY returned vector atomically, revalidates original snapshot source revision/hash/epoch/grant/profile and each vector owner/source/chunk/profile/revision/hash/receipt against current source. Tombstoned/stale/wrong scope candidate is excluded, no fallback/increasedlimit/rescan. If authority/source changes between preflight and hydration -> denied/no matches, not a misleading fresh empty success. At most1 candidate, return one allowlisted Match; zero candidates under current fence -> current matches[]. Caller's limit/model/filter arguments are not accepted. After hydration runner must recheck authority immediately before emitting public summary; if revoked in intervening action gap, withhold. Query transaction is authoritative hydration point, not promise of atomic transaction across asynchronous index search.

Delete/revoke/recovery/purge use the operation-specific ROOT ownership/current expected epoch/historical replay contracts in replay-cleanup.md, never the LIVE inference fence. Fresh owned delete marks source/chunk/vector tombstones atomically, increments source revision/epoch, closes account authority/sourceCurrent/private attachments in same transaction while preserving original known/reserved/active. Subsequent cleanup may physically delete vectors/stage bytes only after evidence hashing, preserving tombstone until root target retirement. Unique owned max1source/vector makes bounded collect limit2 with >1 corruption denial, no global purge. Fresh ROOT revoke sets grant.active=false and grant epoch+1, closes account attachments/live staging authority atomically; already-revoked and exact historical replay are0writes per replay-cleanup.md. ROOT hash-only recovery remains allowed after closure. Wrong tenant/space/owner/grant denies0writes; stale fence cannot delete somebody else's rows.

Negative controls: source revision/hash edited during embedding => E11 denied0insert; duplicate exact write =>0newrows; different receipt/hash=>collision; wrong scope/profile1536/finite shape=>0writes; E12/E13 invocation=>no write function; deletion during embedding=>tombstone survives/no resurrection; source/grant mutation after vectorSearch awaits but before hydrate=>denied no Match; stale candidate =>excluded; wrong index/profile query=>denied before vectorSearch; two unique write rows=>corruption STOP, never choose first. Genuine managed search/native transaction outcomes remain NOT_RUN.

Private evidence table is additionally defined in observer-proofs.md: at most42 records/account (first+2refinements across14 attempts), each <=180000 canonical bytes; no keys/headers/request prompts stored, all access internal. It is a bounded evidence store, not a permit/charge authority. Stage rows max2 per account. Table schema primitives accept numbers/strings but semantic exact parsers impose Epoch/H/private byte limits and zero unknown fields on every handler before database calls; proof IDs never become Convex authorization IDs. A source tombstone is a durable authority fact, not deleted until target retirement.

C3 required immutable ownership metadata for ALL fixture rows: accountHash,targetHash,operatorHash,manifestHash as H fields. Exact StageRow and fixtureLifecycle schemas, DeleteIntent/DeleteResult/RootOwned operations and cleanup cardinality limits are in replay-cleanup.md. LIVE fences never authorize destruction after closure; ROOT lifecycle fences never authorize private read/search/attach or new-stage creation.

C4 fixtureLifecycle rows use exact canonical/preimage/hash fields and row<=65536bytes per hash-recovery.md. ROOT-owned purge retains full nontext triggerCanonical, all lifecycle projections and account tombstones/liability; only private stage/evidence/vector bytes are removed. No recovery tries to invert an aggregate hash.
# Exact receipt and state contract (design, not installed implementation)

All fields below are REQUIRED; null means unavailable, zero means observed zero. Objects have exactly their named own data keys, recursively; no symbols/accessors/prototype/cycles/sparse arrays/ill-formed Unicode/-0/NaN/Infinity. Use accepted C2 canonical.ts descriptor-first detach/sorted-key JSON. Receipt <=8192 UTF8 bytes, graph <=4096 nodes/depth16; string key/values well-formed. Account state <=524288 bytes with same graph bounds (state <=4096 nodes). Larger evidence stays root-private and is represented by digest. No public caller submits receipts or proof labels. The capture boundary revalidates observer classifications using closed proof APIs.

Types: H=lowercase hex64; ID=well-formed nonempty string <=256 UTF8 bytes, no C0/DEL controls; Ref=H (content addressed proof entry, not arbitrary URL); N=integer 0..9007199254740991, no -0. Epoch=N>=1. Time=N (milliseconds UTC). Nullable<T>=T|null. Categories are a sorted unique subset of EXACT enum ["cache-read","cache-write","cancelled","inference","rejected","routing","surcharge"], <=7, no unknown entries; unknown encountered raw categories cause unsupported/STOP and bounded raw digest rather than inventing enum membership.

```ts
interface BindingV2 { manifestHash:H; targetHash:H; sourceHash:H; installedClosureHash:H;
 operatorHash:H; grantHash:H; sourceRecordHash:H; profileHash:H;
 grantEpoch:Epoch; sourceEpoch:Epoch; sourceRevision:Epoch; profileEpoch:Epoch;
 windowEpoch:Epoch; validatorRevision:1 }
interface Counts { input:Nullable<N>; output:Nullable<N> }
interface ReceiptV2 { version:2; evidenceScope:"actual-experiment-native";
 binding:BindingV2; scenarioId:CaseId; dispatchIdentity:H; nativeHash:H;
 expectedWireHash:H; rawDigest:H; method:"generate"|"stream"|"embed";
 interface:"chat"|"embedding"; requestedModel:"openai/gpt-4o-mini"|"openai/text-embedding-3-small";
 responseId:Nullable<ID>; actualModel:Nullable<ID>;
 rawFinish:Nullable<"stop"|"length"|"content_filter">;
 nativeFinish:Nullable<"stop"|"length"|"content-filter"|"tool-calls"|"error"|"other">;
 nativeRawFinish:Nullable<ID>; rawCounts:Counts; mappedCounts:Counts;
 usage:"unknown"|"validated-raw-mapped";
 lifetime:"unknown"|"validated-provider-terminal";
 lifetimeProof:Nullable<Ref>; serving:"unknown"|"validated-bound-premises"|"drift";
 servingProof:Nullable<Ref>; money:"unknown"|"validated-whole-invocation-usd";
 observedCostDecimal:Nullable<ID>; observedCurrency:Nullable<ID>;
 observedCategories:Category[]; microUSD:Nullable<N>; moneyProof:Nullable<Ref>;
 resultHash:Nullable<H>; reason:"none"|"missing-evidence"|"unsupported"|"contradiction"|"bound-violation"|"authority-closed" }
```

ObservedCostDecimal additionally must match /^\d+(\.\d+)?$/ and <=80 chars, is the outward decimal output of pinned conversion (not an untrusted tariff computation). Unknown unsupported numeric observations produce null + rawDigest/reason, not coercion. CaseId EXACT C01..C10/E11..E14 only registered fixed14. Binding and dispatch/native/expectedWire/method/interface/requestedModel match compiled case/account byte-exact. Receipt rawDigest binds complete bounded sanitized observation transcript; raw bytes larger than observer bound yield unknown STOP, never truncated-to-qualified evidence.

Cross-field matrix:

* generate/stream => chat+gpt-4o-mini; embed => embedding+text-embedding-3-small. No interface/model mismatch tolerated. embed rawFinish/nativeFinish/nativeRawFinish all null; output counts may be null or exact0 only. Chat supported raw->unified map stop->stop,length->length,content_filter->content-filter; unknown native raw string retained, supported rawFinish=null and reason unsupported. Tools/reasoning/schema are excluded: tool-calls/error/other never qualifies lifetime in this stage.
* usage validated iff raw input and mapped input present/equal, and Chat raw output and mapped output present/equal; embedding output exact0 is a driver semantic assertion only when raw/mapped input correlation succeeds. Require <=case U/M; missing defaults never count. Contradiction or overbound => unknown+reason contradiction/bound-violation; STOP independently of lifetime. Raw known0 matches mapped0; null does not equal0.
* lifetime validated => nonnull lifetimeProof from resolver; Chat nonnull responseId/actualModel/rawFinish/nativeFinish/nativeRawFinish with exact map/equality; embed nonnull raw responseId/actualModel and source-proven terminal successful shape. Without resolver proof lifetime MUST unknown, proof null. Contradictory evidence is unknown STOP even with installed proof. Genuine qualified terminal with missing usage remains possible; it releases slot, usage failure still STOPs.
* serving validated => nonnull actualModel+servingProof whose record validates all U/M/decoder/output premises. drift => actualModel nonnull and exact mismatch to compiled requested model; servingProof null. Unknown serving => servingProof null. Do not prefix/alias-substitute raw actualModel. Documented alias/revision premises never replace observed ID; exact raw mismatch remains drift even if a tariff proof covers it.
* money validated => microUSD nonnull, observedCostDecimal nonnull, observedCurrency="USD", moneyProof nonnull, observedCategories nonempty; resolver verifies complete whole-invocation aggregate USD/all categories including serving drift. microUSD equals exact outward conversion. money unknown => microUSD null and moneyProof null (observedCostDecimal/currency/categories may still be retained as unqualified facts). A qualified zero must have decimal "0" or exact decimal zero, categories/proof; missing cost never zero.
* reason none only if usage/lifetime/money/serving all validated and resultHash supplied; every other combination must give a non-none reason. Successful raw response without current proof is missing-evidence. Currentness failure closes private authority but cannot discard validated historical charge/terminal facts under historical dispatch-bound proof.

## Stored state

```ts
interface AttemptV2 { scenarioId:CaseId; dispatchIdentity:H; identityCanonical:string;
 state:"dispatch_pending"|"inflight"|"unknown"|"terminal"; checkpoint:true;
 slotReleased:boolean; k:N; known:Nullable<N>;
 firstCapture:Nullable<string>; refinements:string[]; // each ReceiptV2 canonical, <=2
 facts:Facts|null; attachment:"pending"|"attached"|"closed"; privateCanonical:Nullable<string>;
 trigger:"none"|"revoke"|"cancel"; triggerStageHash:Nullable<H>; triggerIdentityHash:Nullable<H> }
interface AccountV2 { version:2; evidenceScope:"actual-experiment-native"; hypothesis:true;
 binding:BindingV2; retainedTriggerCanonical:string; retainedTriggerSetHash:H; next:N; active:Nullable<CaseId>; reserved:N; known:N;
 stopped:boolean; overrun:boolean; revoked:boolean; cancelled:boolean;
 sourceCurrent:boolean; profileCurrent:boolean; proofCurrent:boolean; windowCurrent:boolean;
 attempts:AttemptV2[] }
```

State parser requires exact keys; next0..14, attempts<=14 unique IDs/hash identities matching compiled cases; refinements<=2; firstCapture null iff refinements empty/facts empty; parse all receipt strings recursively; k equals fixed candidate K. Facts is EXACT Omit<ReceiptV2,"rawDigest"|"reason"> plus firstRawDigest:H, refinementRawDigests:H[] (max2), and stopReason:ReceiptV2["reason"]. All other fields have their declared receipt types; classifications are strongest accepted dimensions. Empty facts is null, otherwise fold output, never independently caller-writable. Attempt facts type is Facts|null. firstRawDigest is original receipt.rawDigest; refinementRawDigests exactly ordered accepted refinement digests. stopReason latches first non-none reason, never clears. identityCanonical is exact compiled binding+case canonical (<=65536). privateCanonical null except attached, byte bound/profile validator exact. active is null or exactly the only unreleased attempt; state terminal iff slotReleased. reserved equals sum(k for known=null), known equals sum(known amounts), checked safe arithmetic. next equals attempts.length and attempts follow compiled ORDER; permit identity ordinals remain unchanged. Trigger fields only C09/C10, stage hash and triggerIdentityHash iff trigger non-none; identity hash validated against complete persisted StageIdentity per replay-cleanup.md. stopped/overrun/revoked/cancelled/closed never revert. State graph/canonical bounds failing validation deny all new work; do not overwrite corrupted liability with an empty state. Root must retain corruption digest/account bytes privately for repair review.

## Capture/fact union and writes

Capture parses before update. An invalid first/different receipt commits exactly one account STOP/private-close update, preserves K/known/active/earlier terminal, publishes one account-row update once (format version remains2; Convex OCC, no custom counter); if account is already stopped, attachment closed and active/known/reserved require no transition, any repeated malformed capture returns invalid-retained with zero writes. No malformed receipt overwrites accepted facts. No additional diagnostic ledger is introduced. Contradiction to previously accepted immutable facts is CAPTURE_COLLISION with ZERO writes (earlier STOP/charge/closure remain). Dispatcher catches collision, invokes separate idempotent STOP-control mutation if not already stopped; that mutation one write/closed attachment, no reset. This preserves inherited C2 collision rollback semantics without permitting further dispatch after detected provider contradictions.

Immutable nonnullable fields: version/scope/binding/scenario/dispatch/native/expectedWire/method/interface/requestedModel. For nullable observed facts (responseId, actualModel, raw/native finish, counts, observed cost/currency, resultHash, each proof), once present a later receipt MUST resupply equal values; cannot disappear/change. rawDigest references accumulated transcript, so use firstRawDigest + refinementRawDigests as append-only evidence references in Facts; do not require digest equality when a genuine independent dimension upgrade adds raw evidence. In ReceiptV2 rawDigest is immutable per receipt; prior exact receipt remains replayable. Category facts are an immutable complete sorted observed set once nonempty, never narrowed/expanded in refinement; new raw category creates collision/STOP and separate withheld raw evidence. serving/usage classifications cannot change during capture refinements: observer builds these before first capture, otherwise unknown is irrevocable for this attempt. Their proof/null facts cannot appear later without a lifetime/money dimension upgrade and cannot promote serving readiness on their own.

First receipt stored once. Later exact any historical canonical replay => zero writes. A new receipt requires lifetimeUpgrade (unknown->validated terminal and !released) OR moneyUpgrade (unknown->validated full amount and known=null), max2 refinements. Null facts may fill ONLY alongside one of those independent upgrades, never fact-only. Lifetime/money can't downgrade; a receipt stating unknown after established validated dimension is interpreted as absence of NEW proof only if it resupplies all established observations/proof fields and fold retains known dimension; cross-field parser therefore receives accumulated prior context and validates effective classification, not erasing it. Simpler implementation choice frozen here: later receipt MUST resupply established validated classifications/proofs/amount; this avoids ambiguous downgrade syntax and still permits independent money then lifetime/lifetime then money. Thus full retained known charge stays explicit on later lifetime upgrade. Both upgrades together consume one refinement; third or no-upgrade => collision0writes.

A first unsupported/unknown receipt commits retained liability and STOP, closes attachment permanently. A later permitted proof refinement can settle/release but never clears STOP/reopens private data. A validated terminal releases only its own active slot once; qualified money replaces fullK with full known amount once, never clips >K. Full known on drift requires independent money proof covering exact drift actualModel. Unknown lifetime leaves active even if money known. Unknown money leaves K even if terminal releases slot. All writes use same account-row OCC transaction; no new permit while stopped/active. v1 unchanged nonpaid scope is always denied by v2 parser and v2 denied by original v1 parser.

## Normative parser order

1. Decode JSON with duplicate-object-key rejection; enforce UTF8 byte bound BEFORE parse. Run descriptor-first own-data graph validator, then sorted-key canonical equality to original text. Count nodes/depth and reject sparse/accessor/symbol/proxy-untrusted boundaries as inherited Convex plain-data constraints; never invoke getters.
2. Exact top-level/nested Binding/Counts keys; check enums and N/Epoch/H/ID/null types (boolean never integer); all IDs/strings scalar Unicode and byte bounds. Check category ordering/uniqueness/finite enums; result/proof/digest hashes exact. Version2 scope exact, never infer version from keys. State firstCapture/refinements strings each reenter same receipt parser.
3. Resolve scenario from fixed compiled14 and compare binding/case native/wire/method/interface/model/dispatch against checkpoint; validate counts against c.inputU/maximumOutputM whenever supplied, even if classification unknown. Any overbound becomes retained-invalid STOP, not an accepted unqualified fact hidden from bounds. Result size checked separately against c.conditionalPrivateMaximumBytes; raw evidence byte digest does not establish that bound.
4. Apply complete cross-field matrix above; known amounts require exact decimal rational ceil equality and supported monetary resolver result. State parser recomputes Facts fold/arithmetic/slot owner from immutable accepted receipt sequence; no trusting stored flags/classification. For actual capture, load private transcript and rerun reducer/resolver; a syntactically qualified label with EMPTY/unknown resolver is downgraded to unknown receipt BEFORE storage, removing moneyProof/microUSD and lifetime/serving proof classifications, reason missing-evidence. Preserve observed amounts separately. A false caller label never triggers charge/release. If no prior receipts, publication is conservative STOP1write; if supplied downgrade contradicts prior trusted facts, collision0writes then STOP-control.
5. Union compare before writes; exact canonical historic receipt replay returns0writes before current result-authority checks, but not before immutable dispatch binding. A now-revoked grant does not discard already recorded charge or reopen attachment. Contradictions return collision, not rollback-plus-new-attempt. Invalid integer aggregate arithmetic overflow is STOP/unknown full liability diagnostic; never clamp, wrap or reset. Amounts beyond safe integer representability remain observed decimal/unqualified (unknown money/fullK), not invented known0. Reviewed extension to larger accounting representation would require independent gate.

checks/design-model.py is a pure illustrative SUBSET of schema and branch algebra for hostile examples, not the deployed normative parser or proof authority. It does not claim descriptor-first JavaScript, complete state validation, native semantics or managed transaction execution. Full implementation must satisfy every normative step and unchanged baseline assertions independently.

C3 storage terminology: version=2 is immutable format version; Convex native OCC validates row concurrency, no custom revision counter. Write assertions count committed insert/patch/replace/delete operations and successful transaction publication, not format-version increments. Historical exact replay comparisons precede live delivery/current-grant fences solely for hash-only persistence/recovery.

C4 account exact schema adds retainedTriggerCanonical and retainedTriggerSetHash as required fields; hash-recovery.md defines exact domain/type/order/hash and per-attempt relation before/after purge. These contain no text/vector/raw bytes, stay stable across late lifetime/money refinement and never freeze current L. Fresh internal stage update adds one item atomically with control; all capture/cleanup mutations preserve T byte-exact.
# C4 exact canonical hashes and retained trigger recovery

Design-only finite repair. C3 stage identity/replay precedence/ROOT closed lifecycle authority remain unchanged. This document defines every lifecycle hash preimage, stored redundancy and post-purge relation. Hashes establish content consistency within trusted immutable internal records, never provider serving/money truth, arbitrary-DB-rewrite prevention or proof from a digest alone. No actual proof entry is installed.

## Canonical codec and domain rules

C(x)=accepted descriptor-first canonical own-data JSON: string scalar Unicode, sorted OBJECT keys lexicographically by JS UTF16 code units, JSON.stringify numeric/string encoding, arrays retain declared order, reject duplicate JSON keys/non-own/accessor/symbol/prototype/cycle/sparse/-0/nonfinite. Encode UTF8; H(x)=SHA256(UTF8(C(x))), lowercase64hex. Domain strings below EXACT, version integer1. No timestamp/signer/random salt/header/private text/raw/vector values in hash projections. IDs are valid fixture table IDs verified via corresponding v.id at repository entry; ID strings appear only private retained projections, never public summary. N/Epoch/H/ID limits unchanged. Hash algorithm/codec source pinned in installed closure; no interchangeable JSON canonicalization. All retained canonical strings must equal C(parsed) byte-exact. Graph depth<=16/nodes<=4096 per lifecycle object; retained total row <=65536UTF8bytes. Exact listed keys, no extras.

Scope EXACT {tenantHash:H,spaceHash:H,ownerHash:H}. Owned projection O EXACT {accountHash:H,targetHash:H,manifestHash:H,operatorHash:H,scope:Scope,sourceId:SourceID,chunkId:ChunkID,grantId:GrantID}, derived server-side from immutable installed ownership. Below “owned” always this O, no caller replacement.

### Intent preimages

DeleteIntentCanonical=C({domain:"cortex.experiment.delete-intent.v1",version:1,owned:O,intentKey:H,expectedSourceRevision:Epoch,expectedSourceEpoch:Epoch,expectedGrantEpoch:Epoch}). intentKey equals cleanupKey.

RevokeIntentCanonical=C({domain:"cortex.experiment.revoke-intent.v1",version:1,owned:O,intentKey:H,expectedGrantEpoch:Epoch}). intentKey equals revokeKey.

PurgeIntentCanonical=C({domain:"cortex.experiment.purge-intent.v1",version:1,owned:O,intentKey:H,evidenceSnapshotHash:H}). intentKey equals purgeKey; evidenceSnapshotHash is exact prior returned snapshot, checked freshly for new purge.

intentHash=SHA256(UTF8(the exact intentCanonical)). Domain uniquely determines operation; map delete/revoke/purge to their exact domain, NEVER infer from a caller enum that disagrees. Replay compares complete original canonical preimage, including original expected epochs/snapshot/key, before fresh-effect fences. Existing same operation different key is collision, not a second cleanup authority.

### Immutable trigger projection T

```ts
interface TriggerItem {scenarioId:"C09"|"C10";dispatchIdentity:H;
 trigger:"revoke"|"cancel";stageHash:H;stageIdentityHash:H;
 stageIdentityCanonical:string}
interface TriggerProjection {domain:"cortex.experiment.trigger-set.v1";version:1;
 accountHash:H;bindingHash:H;triggers:TriggerItem[]}
```

bindingHash=H(original compiled BindingV2); triggers max2 unique scenario/dispatch, ordered by original compiled ORDER (C09 before C10). Each stageIdentityCanonical is exact C(StageIdentity) from C3 <=4096bytes, stageIdentityHash its exact digest, nested original binding byte-equal account immutable binding; all redundant TriggerItem fields equal nested identity scenario/dispatch/trigger/stageCanonicalHash. Nested sequence0..511/rawPartDigest H retained. TriggerItem contains full nontext part identity, not privateCanonical/text. stageHash equals nested stageCanonicalHash. triggerSetHash=H(T). Empty set is exact T with triggers:[].

AccountV2 gains REQUIRED retainedTriggerCanonical:string, retainedTriggerSetHash:H, initialized canonical empty T at provisioning. StageAndTrigger fresh effect atomically adds immutable item when it inserts StageRow/control; no subsequent capture/refinement/cleanup may edit an existing item. Max2 with preserved serial/cancel/revoke rules, no new inference capability. Account state parser validates canonical/hash/compiled binding/order and each attempt trigger/triggerStageHash/triggerIdentityHash exactly against T: no missing/extra triggered attempt/item. Before purge, compare complete StageRow identity to T; after purge, compare retained canonical T to purge receipt retained T. ROOT can never create T by merely supplying a hash. Account size524288 bound retained; no custom revision.

### Liability projection L (snapshot, mutable over time)

L EXACT {domain:"cortex.experiment.liability.v1",version:1,accountHash:H,bindingHash:H,next:N,active:CaseId|null,reserved:N,known:N,attempts:LiabilityAttempt[]}.

LiabilityAttempt EXACT {scenarioId:CaseId,dispatchIdentity:H,k:N,known:N|null,state:"dispatch_pending"|"inflight"|"unknown"|"terminal",checkpoint:true,slotReleased:boolean,firstCaptureHash:H|null,refinementHashes:H[]} with <=2 refinement hashes, H(canonical complete accepted ReceiptV2) including original actual/raw facts. attempts <=14, ordered by compiled ORDER admitted prefix, unique dispatch/scenario. L contains NO grant activity/tombstones/attachment flags/private bytes/control trigger fields; those are not monetary/lifetime facts. accountLiabilityHash=H(L). Before/after one delete/revoke/purge MUST produce identical L; later valid historical terminal/money refinement may change current L and hash. Never compare CURRENT L to a stored old L as a recovery validity requirement. Validated full charge/terminal may update known/reserved/active after purge; this neither invalidates T nor authorizes output.

### Lifecycle state snapshot S

S EXACT {domain:"cortex.experiment.lifecycle-state.v1",version:1,owned:O,source:SourceProjection,chunk:ChunkProjection,grant:GrantProjection,vectors:VectorProjection[],flags:Flags,triggerSetHash:H,accountLiabilityHash:H}.

SourceProjection EXACT {sourceId:SourceID,sourceHash:H,revision:Epoch,epoch:Epoch,profileHash:H,tombstone:boolean}.
ChunkProjection EXACT {chunkId:ChunkID,sourceId:SourceID,sourceHash:H,sourceRevision:Epoch,textHash:H,profileHash:H,tombstone:boolean}.
GrantProjection EXACT {grantId:GrantID,grantHash:H,epoch:Epoch,active:boolean}.
VectorProjection EXACT {vectorId:VectorID,sourceId:SourceID,chunkId:ChunkID,sourceRevision:Epoch,sourceHash:H,profileHash:H,dispatchIdentity:H,receiptHash:H,writeKey:H,vectorHash:H,tombstone:boolean}. vectorHash=H({domain:"cortex.experiment.vector.v1",version:1,profileHash:H,vector:number[1536]}), finite/no-0 exact stored vector. vectors max1 sorted by writeKey ascending (tie corrupt). Flags EXACT {stopped:boolean,overrun:boolean,revoked:boolean,cancelled:boolean,sourceCurrent:boolean,profileCurrent:boolean,proofCurrent:boolean,windowCurrent:boolean,attachments:{scenarioId:CaseId,attachment:"pending"|"attached"|"closed"}[]} ordered by admitted compiled ORDER, <=14. No mutable ReceiptV2 facts duplicated outside L. beforeHash=H(S_before); afterHash=H(S_after). Retain both exact canonical S values, treated as HISTORICAL snapshots, not compared to later mutable current state. Fresh effect builds post projection before db writes; commit all or none.

### Evidence projection E

E EXACT {domain:"cortex.experiment.evidence-snapshot.v1",version:1,owned:O,triggerSetHash:H,accountLiabilityHash:H,stages:StageEvidence[],evidence:EvidenceItem[],vectors:VectorEvidence[]}.

StageEvidence EXACT {dispatchIdentity:H,scenarioId:"C09"|"C10",stageIdentityHash:H,stageHash:H,privateBytes:N}; privateBytes=UTF8 exact StageRow.privateCanonical bytes, not exposed text. stages max2 ordered compiled C09,C10; verify stage row identity/T and digest before projecting. EvidenceItem EXACT {dispatchIdentity:H,rawDigest:H,transcriptHash:H,privateBytes:N}; transcriptHash=SHA256(UTF8 exact canonical private transcript), must equal expected rawDigest according to observer serial transcript codec; <=42 items ordered dispatchIdentity then rawDigest lexicographically, unique pair. privateBytes<=180000. VectorEvidence EXACT {writeKey:H,vectorHash:H}; max1 ordered writeKey. No StageRow createdAt/provider timestamp/table physical IDs in E. All stage/evidence/vector row immutable ownership equals O/installed account binding. evidenceSnapshotHash=H(E). E is a bounded SANITIZED projection, not private provider attestation. Retain E canonical in lifecycle row; aggregate digest is not used to reconstruct deleted private content.

## Lifecycle receipt/row and load validation

R EXACT {domain:"cortex.experiment.lifecycle-receipt.v1",version:1,accountHash:H,operation:"delete"|"revoke"|"purge",intentKey:H,intentHash:H,outcome:"applied"|"already-tombstoned"|"already-revoked",beforeHash:H,afterHash:H,evidenceSnapshotHash:H,accountLiabilityHash:H,triggerSetHash:H}. receiptCanonical=C(R); receiptHash=H(R). Public result remains kind+receiptHash only.

fixtureLifecycle row EXACT {accountHash:H,operation:Op,intentKey:H,intentCanonical:string,intentHash:H,receiptCanonical:string,receiptHash:H,beforeCanonical:string,afterCanonical:string,evidenceCanonical:string,liabilityCanonical:string,triggerCanonical:string}; canonical string combined+row <=65536bytes. Convex schema uses v.string for each canonical/hash and exact union operation; semantic parser enforces ALL fields before reads/writes. Domain/version schemas exact; installed ROOT ownership separate. Insert at most1immutable receipt/operation/account. No caller authorizes lifecycle by providing receipt fields.

EVERY load (including history/replay/summary/post-purge) rejects canonical/hash/redundancy mismatch0writes/no summary. Parse exact row and each canonical; recompute intentHash and receiptHash; check row account/operation/key equal intent owned.accountHash/domain/key AND R account/operation/key/intentHash. Recompute H(beforeS),H(afterS),H(E),H(L),H(T) equal R corresponding hashes. S_before/S_after/E/L/T all have same installed account/O/binding where applicable; S/E accountLiabilityHash equals H(L), S/E triggerSetHash equals H(T). Validate nested projection keys/types/order/cardinality and stage identity redundancies, not H regex alone. For purge/delete/revoke stored applied receipt require source/control effect appropriate: delete after.source.tombstone/chunk.tombstone true and source revision/epoch=before+1; revoke after.grant.active false/epoch=before+1; purge after.vectors=[] and private E retained prepurge, no source tombstone/grant changes. Account L unchanged across effect. Staging/evidence removal isn't reconstructed from hashes: authoritative operation receipt plus independently retained T gives exact historical relation. Pre/post flags cannot undo STOP/revoke/cancel or open attachment. Wrong operation domain/table redundancy is corrupt. Auth wrong owner denies before canonical disclosure.

No-write already-tombstoned/already-revoked: fresh current ROOT ownership+expected epoch check, derive exact intent; S_before=S_after CURRENT snapshot, E/L/T current validated snapshots; R outcome corresponding already-* with hashes above; return H(R), zero writes/no row insertion. Repeat same unchanged snapshot yields same hash. Legitimate later accounting may yield different snapshot/hash for another observation; never call it mutation/replay or discard that liability. Stored applied exact replay always returns original immutable R hash even after legitimate later accounting, no stale current-snapshot comparison.

## Post-purge recovery and late accounting

purgeOwnedPrivate validates all existing lifecycle rows and current account T before building E. Fresh purge supplied evidenceSnapshotHash=H(current E); root evidence receipt snapshot taken before call, drift/new late fact changes E/L hash and returns stale0writes rather than silently purging changed snapshot. Fresh purge retains row.triggerCanonical=T and row.liabilityCanonical=L plus E/before/after/R, then deletes ONLY private stage/evidence/vector, preserving source/chunk/account/lifecycle tombstones/facts. Trigger projection is nontext bounded immutable recovery evidence, so postpurge does not invert an aggregate digest.

Postpurge inspectTrigger/recoverOwnedEvidence: validate installed ROOT ownership, EVERY lifecycle row, current account canonical T/hash/attempt relation. Locate valid applied purge receipt, parse its triggerCanonical, require canonical current T EXACT equals retained purge T and H(T)=R.triggerSetHash. Because no new stage is allowed after purge/closure, this immutable set must remain equal. Check account per-attempt trigger/content/identity hashes against corresponding retained complete TriggerItem. Changed sequence/rawDigest/binding/hashes/canonical/extra or missing trigger yields corrupt denial0writes/no summary. No check against old stored L/current known/reserved/active equality; instead revalidate CURRENT accounting parser/fold/refinement rules separately. Thus legitimate late terminal+money changes current L but leaves T fixed and recovery succeeds with current liabilities. New corrupt monetary state also denies via independent accounting parser, not via trigger equality. Missing StageRow before purge with no valid purge receipt remains corrupt. Exact stage persistence replay AFTER purge returns denied closed; inspect may report retained recorded hashes but cannot reconstruct or reopen private stage bytes.

